  "vector_memory": {
    "semantic_summary": "TerrainChunkRenderer is a specialized class inheriting from MeshRendererBehaviour, responsible for rendering a single terrain chunk by directly writing vertex buffers from height data rather than using standard MeshData. It manages multiple LOD levels, calculating the appropriate index buffer based on camera distance via the `chooseLod` function. The component ensures geometry buffers are updated only when the chunk's height version changes, triggering a buffer rewrite via the `refresh` method before rendering."
  },
